---
source: crates/leptoskit_db_macros/src/tests.rs
expression: "report.join(\"\\n\")"
---
no name: a table needs an explicit name, such as #[db::table(name = "users")]: renaming the struct then never renames the table
unknown table option: unknown table option; expected `name`, `namespace`, `public`, `projection`, `index`, `unique`, `check`, `renamed_from`, `pack`, or `crate`
check without sql: `check` needs both `name = "..."` and `sql = "..."`
check with an unknown part: `check` takes `name = "..."` and `sql = "..."`
empty index: name at least one field, such as `index(author_id, created_at)`
derived Serialize: don't derive `Serialize` on a table: rows never cross the wire; return the generated public type (`Public…`) from server functions
derived Debug: don't derive `Debug` on a table: leptoskit generates `Debug` so that `secret` columns are redacted
generic: a table can't be generic
tuple: a table needs named fields: one per column
no key: a table needs a primary key: add `pub id: Id<Self>`, or mark the key fields with #[db(key)]
unknown column option: unknown column option; expected one of `key`, `generate`, `column`, `unique`, `index`, `private`, `secret`, `default`, `min_len`, `max_len`, `min`, `max`, `one_of`, `regex`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`, `version`, `on_delete`, `on_soft_delete`, `backlink`, `no_foreign_key`, `renamed_from`, `flatten`, `prefix`, `in`, or `generated`
bad regex: `regex` isn't a valid regular expression: regex parse error:
    (
    ^
error: unclosed group
bad on_delete: `on_delete` is one of `cascade`, `set_null`, `restrict`, `no_action`, or `deferred_restrict`
bad default: a default is a literal, `now`, or `default(sql = "...")`
bad default literal: a default is a string, number, or boolean literal
default with an unknown part: `default(...)` takes `sql = "..."`
unique with an unknown part: `unique` takes `except = field`, the soft-delete column
unique except a missing field: `User` has no field `gone`
generated key that isn't Id<Self>: only a single `Id<Self>` key can be generated; set the key yourself with #[db(key, generate = false)]
two created_at: only one column can be #[db(created_at)]
timestamp key: a key can't also be a timestamp or a version
